{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Why does my lord speak such words, etc. Indeed, the silver that we found in the mouth of our sacks we brought back to you; how then could we steal?</b> This is the inference from minor to major (קל וחומר) that the Sages, of blessed memory, derived — among the ten inferences from minor to major found in the Torah: if we returned what we found, all the more so that we would not steal."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:07.413461954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}